\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}Standard number systems are $\mathbb N,\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$. Specialized notation and index ranges follow the cited source and the definitions below.


A symbolic deduction system specifies inference rules that can be checked exactly. A neural model supplies statistical pattern predictions; an agent architecture combines these with a procedure for selecting tasks, tools, and candidate deductions.
\paragraph{Record scope and qualifications.}
The catalogue title is retained as metadata. Named certificates, contracts, bounds or frameworks in that title are not asserted as results of the original source extract.
This is a system-design and benchmark direction. No definite mathematical correctness, novelty, or performance theorem is stated.

Source-record limitation: An autonomous research-agent architecture and benchmark performance are requested without a mathematical statement.
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Build an agentic AI system that carries out the full workflow of a mathematician, from exploring examples and formulating conjectures to selecting proof strategies, and determine whether it can solve research-level benchmarks such as FATE-X autonomously. Identify an effective architecture that combines neural pattern recognition with rigorous symbolic deduction to produce novel, human-readable, formally checkable proofs. \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2025/43}{[S2]}
\paragraph{Source status.}
The supplied catalogue labels this source record open; that metadata was checked against the supplied snapshot on 2026-10-11. The label is preserved for provenance and is not an independent verification of present open status or mathematical correctness. The catalogue literature assessment is dated 2026-08-22.

